{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>From every sin of a person</b> — juxtaposed to the sending out of the impure. For through the sin of the person that the first man sinned by eating from the tree, and the serpent deceived the woman and brought disrepute upon man — the three were struck: the serpent with tzara'at, the woman with zav, and man with death. And in the order of their curse, they are enumerated here: מצורע — that is, the serpent; זב — that is, the woman; and טמא לנפש — that is, the man, who was punished with מות תמות." "<b>ל</b> — מעול מעל. [The letter] lamed [in] בה'. To teach that whoever perverts judgment below [in an earthly court], it is as if he perverts the judgment of Above." "<b>That person</b> — and they shall confess. A hint that all who are executed make confession at the time of the soul's departure."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:07.447069951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}